- Complete man/writeZarrArray-auto-args.Rd

- Report the following problem: Rarr::read_zarr_array() chokes when using
  an "empty index" on a Zarr v3 dataset. For example:

    library(Rarr)

    zarr_v2 <- system.file(package="Rarr", "extdata",
                           "zarr_examples", "column-first", "int32.zarr")
    read_zarr_array(zarr_v2, list(integer(0), integer(0), integer(0)))  # ok
    read_zarr_array(zarr_v2, list(integer(0), NULL, 1))  # ok

    zarr_v3 <- system.file(package="Rarr", "extdata",
                           "zarr_examples", "column-first", "int32_v3.zarr")
    read_zarr_array(zarr_v3, list(integer(0), integer(0), integer(0)))  # error!
    read_zarr_array(zarr_v3, list(integer(0), NULL, 1))  # error!

- ZarrArraySeed() and ZarrArray() should support Zarr datasets on S3.
  Note that Rarr::read_zarr_array(), the workhorse behind the extract_array()
  method for ZarrArraySeed objects, already supports datasets stored on S3.

- writeZarrArray() needs to write the array dimnames to disk.

- Add support for sparse Zarr datasets.

- Improve support for Zarr v3.


After ZarrArray is accepted and added to BioC 3.23
==================================================

- Remove the underscore prefix from our class names after the corresponding
  classes in Rarr are gone.

- Register realization backend _ZarrArray in the DelayedArray package.

- Implement saveZarrSummarizedExperiment() and
  loadZarrSummarizedExperiment() for saving/loading
  a Zarr-based SummarizedExperiment object to/from disk.

